<title>NETHERLANDS: Baan details $175 mln convertible.</title>
<headline>Baan details $175 mln convertible.</headline>
<dateline>EDE, Netherlands 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer software firm Baan Company NV said it was issuing $175 million of convertible subordinated notes due 2001. The notes have a 4.5 percent coupon and are convertible into common shares of Baan at a price of $44 per share.</p>
<p>Baan said the proceeds of the issue would be used among other things for further international expansion and a higher level of research and development activity.</p>
<p>Additionally some of the proceeds might be used to acquire complementary businesses, products or technologies, it said.</p>
